last:
As I, with all my blots: with all my blots!
At last then, peerless cousin, we are peers—
At last we’re even. Ah, you’ve left your height;

lashing:
New gales of tropic fury round my head
Break lashing me through hours of soulful dread;
But when the terror thins and, spent, withdraws,

Would scare the writer if they splashed the mud
In lashing off the flies,—didactics, driven
Against the heels of what the master said;

lasted:
Love was pleasant enough, and the days went fast;
Pleasant while it lasted, but it needn't last;
Awhile on the wax and awhile on the wane,

lasting:
To slacken all those bonds which seemed too soon
And quickly tied to make a lasting troth.
Quick-loving hearts, I thought, may quickly loathe;

lashed:
A wind sprang up from the ends of the earth;
It lashed the forest together.
A huge green wave thundered and burst over my head.

lashes:
He should seek my doorstep, pale with need?
There could he lie, and dry would be my lashes;
Let him stop his noise, and let me read.

las:
Nigh enough to hyeah de noises in de road;
Fu' I t'ink de las' long res'
Gwine to soothe my sperrit bes'

lasses:
The ripples wimple on the rills,
Like sparkling little lasses;
The sunlight runs along the hills,

lashin:
Have to feel mine evah minute to be sho' I got it daih;
En' de win' is cuttin' capahs an' a-lashin' thoo de trees,
But de rain keeps on a-singin' blessed songs, lak "Tek yo' ease."

